WEBVTT

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.542
So he's taken the students hostage.

00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:16.917
I'm betting...

00:00:16.917 --> 00:00:20.792
...he means to lure me in and then kill me.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.333
Well, shucks.

00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:29.208
That sure throws a wrench into my plans.

00:00:29.208 --> 00:00:31.292
Koro Sensei and Mr. Karasuma!

00:00:31.292 --> 00:00:34.000
But Koro Sensei was in Brazil!

00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:38.917
Oh, well. Plan 16 it is.

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:41.125
My time to shine.

00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:51.583
Wh-What's this?!

00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:53.417
The whole room is going down!

00:00:57.208 --> 00:00:58.750
Irina!

00:01:13.542 --> 00:01:16.208
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:19.042
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:01:19.042 --> 00:01:24.458
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:01:24.458 --> 00:01:27.125
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:29.833
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:33.625
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:37.625
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:40.583
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:45.792
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:01:45.792 --> 00:01:51.417
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:56.833
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:01:56.833 --> 00:02:02.333
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:04.958
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.625
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:02:07.625 --> 00:02:10.417
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:13.000
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.708
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:18.417
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:21.250
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.208
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:02:29.958 --> 00:02:34.000
"Eighth Period: Reaper Time, Part 2"
"by Ryoma Terasaka"

00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:40.167
Not you, too, Miss Irina...

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:42.375
You're behind all this?

00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:46.792
Does the name "the Reaper" ring a bell?

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:49.417
I've heard of it, from Lovro.

00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:51.875
I let him live on purpose.

00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:54.750
If I want my competitors to leave the game,

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.500
I need him to spread the word about me.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:01.125
Hey, how about lowering that gun?

00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:03.750
Or should I shoot your friend here?

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.542
The way he obscures his presence...

00:03:09.292 --> 00:03:13.625
I've put explosives on her neck
and on the students' necks.

00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:16.667
I just give the high sign and they'll detonate.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:21.500
You think if you threaten
your hostages, I'll die quietly?

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.000
Now, I wonder!

00:03:25.292 --> 00:03:27.208
I don't sense anyone else around.

00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:29.500
If I'm just careful with his gun...

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.375
But why...?

00:03:44.458 --> 00:03:46.000
M-My tentacles...

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.042
He can see them?!

00:03:49.625 --> 00:03:51.917
--Koro Sensei!
--Are you okay?

00:03:51.917 --> 00:03:53.625
That was disappointingly quick.

00:03:53.625 --> 00:03:56.583
I didn't even have to use the hostages.

00:03:57.125 --> 00:04:01.000
Let's go say goodbye.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.792
Miss Irina...

00:04:02.792 --> 00:04:04.167
Sir!

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.667
Class...

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:08.292
Is everyone unhurt?

00:04:08.292 --> 00:04:11.292
I can't believe he captured you, too.

00:04:13.542 --> 00:04:17.000
Bars made of anti-me material, eh?

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.375
It's tricky stuff, to be sure...

00:04:19.375 --> 00:04:22.667
...but my body has finally overcome it!

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.625
Really?!

00:04:26.292 --> 00:04:31.875
Now to reveal to you...
my secret internal-organ weapon!

00:04:34.458 --> 00:04:37.292
I made this tongue with
a coating of digestive juices.

00:04:37.292 --> 00:04:39.958
Give me half a day
and I can lick these bars away.

00:04:39.958 --> 00:04:41.250
Too slow!

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.250
Say...

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:47.167
Keep licking like that and
I'll detonate everyone's neckbombs.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.125
What? Aw!

00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:52.458
Now, then--better hurry.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:55.667
I'm about to flood this place with water.

00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:57.625
This is a drainage canal.

00:04:57.625 --> 00:05:00.292
On my command
from the control room up above,

00:05:00.292 --> 00:05:03.917
200 tons of water per second

00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:07.708
will squeeze you
into noodles against these bars.

00:05:07.708 --> 00:05:10.542
Wait! You intend to kill the students, too?

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.708
Of course. It's too late to wait.

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:17.792
Irina! You knew as much, and yet...

00:05:17.792 --> 00:05:20.792
As a pro, I just
prioritized results, that's all.

00:05:20.792 --> 00:05:23.708
Isn't that what you wanted?

00:05:23.708 --> 00:05:26.208
True, it may be a little harsh...

00:05:26.208 --> 00:05:30.833
Or should I let our best chance of
saving the world slip away before our eyes?

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:37.583
Say there comes a time we can kill him
in exchange for the students' lives.

00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:40.292
What is the government's policy on that?

00:05:40.292 --> 00:05:44.542
Well, that's, uh... you'd handle that
on a case-by-case basis.

00:05:44.542 --> 00:05:49.125
It may actually come down
to that situation, and, uh...

00:05:49.125 --> 00:05:53.708
J-Just make that decision at the scene.

00:05:53.708 --> 00:05:57.958
So it's my responsibility, in effect.

00:05:57.958 --> 00:06:02.042
Then my decision now...

00:06:02.042 --> 00:06:04.667
Here's how the government sees it.

00:06:07.458 --> 00:06:11.208
The lives of 27 people
are weightier than the Earth.

00:06:11.208 --> 00:06:15.083
If you still plan on killing them, too...

00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:17.250
...I'll stop you.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:21.250
--Mr. Karasuma!
--S-So cool!

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:24.042
And I'll tell you this, Irina:

00:06:24.042 --> 00:06:27.167
Being a pro isn't quite so carefree.

00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:33.708
If it takes too long to kill Karasuma,
my plans will come apart.

00:06:33.708 --> 00:06:35.333
And so...

00:06:36.208 --> 00:06:37.208
I don't think so!

00:06:37.208 --> 00:06:38.583
Mr. Karasuma!

00:06:38.583 --> 00:06:41.208
Turn on your transceiver!

00:06:42.667 --> 00:06:46.292
Hmph. How rash.

00:06:46.292 --> 00:06:49.333
Karasuma may stand apart from others...

00:06:49.333 --> 00:06:51.250
...but <i>he </i>goes even further.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:54.542
Just look at how easily
he trapped that octopus.

00:06:54.542 --> 00:06:56.917
Professor Bitch...

00:06:57.958 --> 00:07:00.708
Irina, I need your help.

00:07:00.708 --> 00:07:02.792
I've set a trap.

00:07:02.792 --> 00:07:05.458
While Karasuma's fiddling with it,

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.667
shoot him from behind.

00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:10.417
Understood.

00:07:16.458 --> 00:07:20.583
The other side of this
doorknob feels wrong. A trap?

00:07:20.583 --> 00:07:23.125
No time to disarm it.

00:07:23.125 --> 00:07:25.458
Guess I'll just open it.

00:07:28.125 --> 00:07:32.333
Did that get him?
It'll slow him down, anyway.

00:07:38.917 --> 00:07:42.792
Tsk. More powerful than I'd expected.

00:07:57.667 --> 00:08:02.625
Your nose for bloodlust is spot on.
I admit--I underestimated you.

00:08:02.625 --> 00:08:06.875
It's like a trade fair for traps. Well done.

00:08:06.875 --> 00:08:09.792
Once you master the skills to kill a person,

00:08:09.792 --> 00:08:13.792
it's in an assassin's nature
to want to use every last one of them.

00:08:15.708 --> 00:08:18.042
Make sure you hit him, Irina.

00:08:18.042 --> 00:08:19.875
Sorry.

00:08:19.875 --> 00:08:22.417
This next one will.

00:08:23.292 --> 00:08:25.667
You're going to die, Irina.

00:08:25.667 --> 00:08:28.167
I'm more than prepared for that.

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:32.875
You probably can't understand, but he does.

00:08:32.875 --> 00:08:35.667
"You and I are the same," he said.

00:08:35.667 --> 00:08:40.375
That's right--did I tell you my backstory?

00:08:40.375 --> 00:08:43.375
Born in a poor slum beset by
constant terrorist attacks,

00:08:43.375 --> 00:08:46.750
an uncertain world where
life could blink out in an instant.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.750
I could trust only in
money and my own skills...

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.125
...and that if you kill people, they die.

00:08:53.125 --> 00:08:57.542
And so Irina understands how I feel.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:09.583
Right, Irina? Even if
I <i>did </i>use you as a sacrifice.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.000
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Karma Akabane"

00:09:24.083 --> 00:09:25.917
You're alive!

00:09:25.917 --> 00:09:27.792
I should have known.

00:09:27.792 --> 00:09:30.458
But you can't come after me.

00:09:30.458 --> 00:09:37.000
You know...
I only hired her to deceive you all.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.250
Irina...

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:43.250
Well, time for the big finish.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.750
Wait!

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.375
Mis... ra... ma!

00:09:46.375 --> 00:09:47.833
Mr. Karasuma!

00:09:47.833 --> 00:09:50.125
Are you all right?!

00:09:50.125 --> 00:09:50.875
What is it?

00:09:50.875 --> 00:09:55.000
I finally got through.
What was that explosion?

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.583
I'm all right, but Irina's
trapped under the debris.

00:09:59.417 --> 00:10:02.208
I don't have time for that.
I'm going after the Reaper.

00:10:02.208 --> 00:10:03.833
You can't!

00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:07.542
Why won't you help her, Mr. Karasuma?

00:10:07.542 --> 00:10:10.542
Kurahashi...

00:10:10.542 --> 00:10:15.167
Irina partnered with the Reaper
to get results in her own way.

00:10:15.167 --> 00:10:18.375
A real pro accepts her own responsibility.

00:10:18.375 --> 00:10:20.625
What's being a pro have to do with it?

00:10:20.625 --> 00:10:23.333
I know this is coming from a 15-year-old...

00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:26.375
but Professor Bitch is only 21!

00:10:27.542 --> 00:10:32.833
Growing up in an environment
with no peace of mind,

00:10:32.833 --> 00:10:36.625
she probably forgot to pick up
some of the pieces along the way

00:10:36.625 --> 00:10:40.250
that would make her a grown-up.

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:44.667
So please... rescue her, Mr. Karasuma.

00:10:44.667 --> 00:10:49.375
Just like you forgive us students
when <i>we </i>make mistakes.

00:10:54.042 --> 00:10:57.083
The village is wiped out.

00:10:57.083 --> 00:11:00.708
But this one killed
a militia member and escaped.

00:11:00.708 --> 00:11:03.167
What do you think, dear?

00:11:06.875 --> 00:11:08.708
Good eyes.

00:11:10.375 --> 00:11:13.250
You have a decision to make:

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:16.708
If you live in blood with us,

00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:22.167
your hideous memories of blood
can become just another routine.

00:11:22.167 --> 00:11:27.375
You can seek peaceful days,
living in fear of your blood memories,

00:11:27.375 --> 00:11:31.542
or, rather than running from them,
tame your memories through work.

00:11:34.125 --> 00:11:39.500
A cruel choice for a child.
Let's go to the refugee camp and--

00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:43.583
There's no turning back.

00:11:46.167 --> 00:11:48.750
That's right.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:53.292
A cold sea of blood was my everyday.

00:11:53.292 --> 00:11:56.208
How fitting that I should die betrayed.

00:11:58.708 --> 00:12:00.958
I'm glad it can end...

00:12:00.958 --> 00:12:06.292
...before I remember the warmth...
of a place in the sun...

00:12:12.833 --> 00:12:17.875
Get on out of there.
I'll handle the heavy lifting.

00:12:21.417 --> 00:12:23.833
What's this...?

00:12:23.833 --> 00:12:27.125
They've all escaped!

00:12:27.125 --> 00:12:31.958
No matter. I'll just kill a couple-few
and threaten them over the intercom.

00:12:33.875 --> 00:12:35.917
They took them off?!

00:12:35.917 --> 00:12:37.667
Wow, they're good!

00:12:37.667 --> 00:12:39.083
Damn.

00:12:39.958 --> 00:12:44.000
The bombs' remote only has a detonate
command and an unlock function.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:47.833
So simple that they won't
explode if we pull them off,

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:49.917
and he'll never know.

00:12:49.917 --> 00:12:51.667
Th-This is rough...

00:12:51.667 --> 00:12:55.958
This protective coloring matches the walls,
and the light quality is just right!

00:12:55.958 --> 00:13:00.292
Just like you said, there's a spot
the camera can't see properly!

00:13:00.292 --> 00:13:02.208
Then, with Sugaya's spray...

00:13:02.208 --> 00:13:05.542
That assassination camo
works great on our super P.E. clothes.

00:13:05.542 --> 00:13:07.875
We can make 'em perfectly wall-colored!

00:13:07.875 --> 00:13:13.292
Sheesh... who knew the RC peeping squad
would play such a big role?

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:15.333
What about Koro Sensei?

00:13:15.333 --> 00:13:17.792
He's got protective coloring built in.

00:13:17.792 --> 00:13:20.500
Which means he's buck naked right now.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.208
Now I can never get married!

00:13:22.208 --> 00:13:24.792
Quit blushing or he'll see you!

00:13:27.042 --> 00:13:31.792
Your left arm may be broken.

00:13:31.792 --> 00:13:33.875
Does it hurt anywhere else?

00:13:34.875 --> 00:13:36.208
Hey, you're bleeding!

00:13:36.208 --> 00:13:39.875
No--your super-hot body just got me excited.

00:13:39.875 --> 00:13:42.042
I thought you might have brain damage,

00:13:42.042 --> 00:13:44.875
but that's perfectly normal for you.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:49.750
He's back. Just as the students had predicted.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:55.667
Irina, this may be different
from the world you grew up in,

00:13:55.667 --> 00:14:00.750
but the world that the students
and I live in... it needs you.

00:14:09.917 --> 00:14:12.208
Irina, where's Karasuma?

00:14:12.208 --> 00:14:15.750
He was already gone when I came to.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.042
That was awful of you, Reaper,

00:14:18.042 --> 00:14:21.083
blowing me up, too.

00:14:21.083 --> 00:14:23.000
Yeah, sorry about that!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:26.792
I wouldn't've been able
to achieve my goal otherwise.

00:14:26.792 --> 00:14:30.500
Besides, our world is one
of deceiving and being deceived.

00:14:32.958 --> 00:14:39.250
Oh, I don't mind. After all,
I'm a bitch who hops from man to man.

00:14:43.333 --> 00:14:46.667
I-Is this guy nuts?

00:14:48.292 --> 00:14:53.000
I've been thinking. Are you really
all you're cracked up to be?

00:14:57.625 --> 00:14:59.708
What was that?

00:15:05.667 --> 00:15:08.625
Each one of your skills is on point,

00:15:08.625 --> 00:15:11.292
but your endgame and defenses are weak.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:17.417
You sure told me.

00:15:17.417 --> 00:15:19.375
You--

00:15:19.375 --> 00:15:22.208
I peeled off my face.

00:15:22.208 --> 00:15:26.583
It just gets in the way
of improving my disguise skills.

00:15:26.583 --> 00:15:31.750
Now to kill you and take <i>your </i>face!

00:15:37.375 --> 00:15:39.083
Hey, what's going on?

00:15:39.083 --> 00:15:40.250
Um, er...

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.375
The Reaper has a knife--no, a wire!

00:15:42.375 --> 00:15:43.917
He uses that on Mr. Karasuma, and--oh, wow!

00:15:43.917 --> 00:15:46.417
He blocks with his elbow--no good. Eek!

00:15:46.417 --> 00:15:48.167
He's using his knife
as a shield, and seeing that,

00:15:48.167 --> 00:15:50.417
he switched to a kick, but at the same time...!

00:15:50.417 --> 00:15:52.875
What a... what a <i>great fight</i>!

00:15:52.875 --> 00:15:53.042
What the <i>heck </i>are you saying?!

00:15:53.042 --> 00:15:54.458
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #29: Gives terrible play-by-plays"
What the <i>heck </i>are you saying?!

00:15:54.458 --> 00:15:55.500
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #29: Gives terrible play-by-plays"
Mmm?!

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:57.292
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #29: Gives terrible play-by-plays"
Explain it so we understand!

00:15:57.292 --> 00:15:57.833
Explain it so we understand!

00:15:57.833 --> 00:16:00.083
I dared to pull him into close-quarters combat,

00:16:00.083 --> 00:16:04.583
but I don't know what he's hiding.
Can't let this drag on.

00:16:06.833 --> 00:16:09.750
I'll tell you the truth, Mr. Karasuma.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:13.583
I made up that part about
growing up in tragic circumstances.

00:16:13.583 --> 00:16:17.083
That was social engineering,
to pull the woman in.

00:16:17.083 --> 00:16:19.083
Why, you...

00:16:19.083 --> 00:16:22.833
An assassin killed my father.

00:16:23.917 --> 00:16:27.000
I wasn't particularly sad that he was dead.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:31.708
But the movements of the killer
who cut him down before my eyes

00:16:31.708 --> 00:16:34.167
made me think:

00:16:34.167 --> 00:16:37.833
What a beautiful skill!

00:16:39.625 --> 00:16:45.625
I was captivated. Assassination:
an ensemble of beautiful skills!

00:16:46.875 --> 00:16:50.958
And the essence of those skills I mastered?

00:16:50.958 --> 00:16:53.125
Allow me to show you:

00:16:59.292 --> 00:17:02.167
The Reaper's hidden scythe.

00:17:02.167 --> 00:17:04.167
Just a .10 caliber.

00:17:04.167 --> 00:17:11.125
Its minute bullets pass between muscle
and bone to tear a hole in the aorta.

00:17:11.125 --> 00:17:16.792
The aorta's own bloodstream
pressure widens that hole...

00:17:16.792 --> 00:17:21.417
...until you die from major blood loss.

00:17:21.417 --> 00:17:26.458
A composite art only the Reaper can pull off.

00:17:28.042 --> 00:17:30.042
What?!

00:17:30.042 --> 00:17:31.625
Is this...

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:40.083
Finally, a definitive opening.

00:17:40.083 --> 00:17:43.708
Good to see even the Reaper
has the same weak spots.

00:17:43.708 --> 00:17:45.708
Is that the octopus's...

00:17:45.708 --> 00:17:47.417
"Tomato Juice"

00:17:47.875 --> 00:17:51.458
I can just about fit <i>one </i>tentacle through.

00:17:51.458 --> 00:17:55.042
You were dummied up with <i>juice</i>?

00:17:55.042 --> 00:17:58.375
Ready, Reaper?

00:17:58.375 --> 00:18:02.792
You messed with my
precious students and colleagues.

00:18:02.792 --> 00:18:06.917
Wait! Who else could kill him, if not me?!

00:18:06.917 --> 00:18:11.417
Our classroom has all the skills we need!

00:18:16.333 --> 00:18:19.083
Why don't you quit the killing game?

00:18:19.083 --> 00:18:23.667
Your skills will come in handy
at the employment office.

00:18:31.167 --> 00:18:35.958
The man had marvelous skills,
but put too much faith in them.

00:18:35.958 --> 00:18:39.208
Whoever influenced him was a fool.

00:18:39.208 --> 00:18:42.958
He could have used his skills
to follow a much straighter path.

00:18:42.958 --> 00:18:45.208
Sparing people or killing them...

00:18:45.208 --> 00:18:48.083
It's all up to the person
and the world around them.

00:18:48.083 --> 00:18:49.917
Yes, exactly.

00:18:49.917 --> 00:18:51.875
Right, Miss Irina?

00:18:51.875 --> 00:18:53.292
Urk!

00:18:57.292 --> 00:18:58.333
You bitch!

00:18:58.333 --> 00:19:00.292
What's the big idea, tryin' to run away?!

00:19:00.292 --> 00:19:01.917
Eeek!

00:19:01.917 --> 00:19:02.833
Ow!

00:19:02.833 --> 00:19:05.042
Argh! Just do whatever you want!

00:19:05.042 --> 00:19:07.250
The boys with their usual pent-up animal lust,

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:09.625
the girls with their usual envy of my beauty--

00:19:09.625 --> 00:19:13.458
just let it all out in
an explosion of sexual violence!

00:19:13.458 --> 00:19:15.708
Her ideas are getting wild!

00:19:15.708 --> 00:19:18.583
Look, just come to school like always.

00:19:18.583 --> 00:19:21.250
No more shirkin' your duties for days on end.

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:23.750
I'm dying to know more about that story--

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:27.750
swindling Arabian royalty
until you were on the brink of war!

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:28.750
If you don't come back,

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:33.625
I'll just keep that French
<i>Boys Over Flowers </i>manga you lent me!

00:19:33.625 --> 00:19:37.458
You know I was this close to killing you all.

00:19:37.458 --> 00:19:40.000
Is that a problem?

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:45.917
Backstabbing, treachery...
Isn't that what makes you a bitch?

00:19:45.917 --> 00:19:49.208
And if we can't even
enjoy school with a bitch,

00:19:49.208 --> 00:19:53.500
what are we doing being
junior-high assassins, anyway?

00:19:54.375 --> 00:19:56.750
That's right.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:04.417
This flower wasn't
borrowed from our students.

00:20:04.417 --> 00:20:07.792
I came by it intentionally,
by defeating the enemy.

00:20:07.792 --> 00:20:11.083
Is that good enough for your birthday?

00:20:11.083 --> 00:20:15.583
He hands it over so blandly!
And there are way fewer flowers this time!

00:20:15.583 --> 00:20:17.708
I'll give him a piece of my mind!

00:20:17.708 --> 00:20:22.750
Now, what do you say
at a time like this? Let's see here...

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:26.083
Yes.

00:20:26.083 --> 00:20:28.625
Ooh, we have potential!

00:20:28.625 --> 00:20:31.417
But I had dibs!

00:20:31.417 --> 00:20:32.750
There, there.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:36.708
Mr. Karasuma, a word before
things take a turn for the racy?

00:20:36.708 --> 00:20:39.250
It definitely won't, but please.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:45.750
I don't want the students
involved in this kind of danger again.

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:53.000
I must insist on an environment
where we can safely kill and be killed.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.042
I know.

00:20:55.042 --> 00:20:56.042
"If any student becomes collateral damage during an assassination,

00:20:56.042 --> 00:20:57.750
"Ministry of Defense"
"If any student becomes collateral damage during an assassination,

00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:58.083
"If any student becomes collateral damage during an assassination,

00:20:58.083 --> 00:21:01.333
the bounty will not be paid." Hmm.

00:21:01.333 --> 00:21:02.667
"Request" "Students of E Class"
the bounty will not be paid." Hmm.

00:21:02.667 --> 00:21:06.875
"Request" "Students of E Class"
You've really grown fond of those kids, eh, Karasuma?

00:21:06.875 --> 00:21:11.208
Surely the students
have a right to their safety.

00:21:11.208 --> 00:21:14.125
All right. I'll accept these conditions.

00:21:14.125 --> 00:21:20.125
Either way, we're done
relying on individual freelance killers.

00:21:20.125 --> 00:21:22.750
We're jointly moving forward

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:25.833
with the final assassination project.

00:21:33.375 --> 00:21:37.958
I don't know where this classroom is headed...

00:21:42.375 --> 00:21:47.875
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>
<i>  </i>

00:21:47.875 --> 00:21:48.458
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>
<i>  </i>

00:21:48.458 --> 00:21:49.625
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>
Your arm?

00:21:49.625 --> 00:21:51.542
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>
Fine.

00:21:51.542 --> 00:21:53.250
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>
But this place... is a good world to be in.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:56.958
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>
But this place... is a good world to be in.

00:21:56.958 --> 00:21:58.917
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:58.917 --> 00:22:04.083
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:22:04.083 --> 00:22:15.458
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:22:15.458 --> 00:22:21.042
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:22:21.042 --> 00:22:25.458
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:25.458 --> 00:22:32.292
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:32.292 --> 00:22:37.792
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:37.792 --> 00:22:43.292
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:43.292 --> 00:23:02.102
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>
